---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What counts as a campaign?',
    a: 'One contracted media buy with a defined flight period: a set of creatives, publishers, and expected placements, finished and published. The standard scope is up to 5 creatives across up to 20 publishers and 40 episodes, including historical lookback. A campaign is one insertion order, whether it runs on three shows or eight; two separate insertion orders are two campaigns.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What do you need from us?',
    a: 'Three things. The master creative files, one per contracted version, the exact cuts that were supposed to air. The placement plan or insertion order, so we know what "correct delivery" means. And access to the published media, which usually means nothing more than the public RSS feeds, plus any recordings you already hold if you want them included. We confirm scope and sources with you before starting.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if a placement is ambiguous?',
    a: 'It is classified as Insufficient Signal or Manual Review Required, and the report tells you which and why. An episode published at low bitrate, or with heavy talk-over on the creative, can be genuinely undecidable, and we report that honestly rather than leaning on a borderline score. Flagged placements are examined by a person before the report ships. You are never shown a number that is quietly a guess.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you verify dynamic ad insertion?',
    a: 'Not in V1. DAI placements vary per listener, so the published feed often does not contain the ad that any individual heard, and honest verification requires a different evidence model, for example server logs or a measurement integration. We verify pre-produced audio creatives in podcast and digital audio where the published media is independently observable. If your campaign is DAI-heavy we will tell you at scoping that we are the wrong tool for it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this legal proof?',
    a: 'No, and anyone who sells you "court-ready" ad verification should be asked hard questions. A Meyppi audit is evidence: documented, repeatable findings with confidence levels, hashes, and a written methodology. That is the right standard for reconciling with a publisher, supporting a makegood, or reporting to a client. Courts set their own standards, and we do not claim to meet them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does an audit take?',
    a: 'Five to ten working days from receiving the creatives and media access, for a standard single campaign. The compute is fast, over 1,000 audio-minutes per CPU-hour; the time goes into collecting sources and manually reviewing flagged placements, which is where accuracy actually comes from. Historical lookback adds days rather than weeks, depending on what the feeds still serve. If a source turns out to be unreachable we tell you immediately and you decide whether to proceed with reduced scope.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if the audit finds nothing wrong?',
    a: 'Then you have bought certainty, which is what most audits find. The report is identical in format either way: every placement classified, evidence attached. A clean report has real value in client reviews and internal sign-off, and we do not shade the process toward finding problems, because a verification company that needs discrepancies is a verification company with a conflict of interest.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who sees the results?',
    a: 'Only you. The audit is commissioned by you and delivered to you. We do not publish findings, share campaign data with publishers, or use your material in case studies without written permission. Creative files and media are processed solely to produce your report and are handled per the privacy policy.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Pricing"
  description="Fixed-fee campaign audits from ₹15,000. No annual contracts, no hidden usage charges."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Pricing</span>
      <h1>A fixed quote for each campaign.</h1>
      <p class="section__lede">
        The quote is agreed in writing before work starts. Most audits
        fall between ₹15,000 and ₹25,000 plus applicable taxes. No annual
        contracts, no hidden usage charges.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid--2 pricing-grid">
        <div class="card card--accent plan reveal">
          <span class="kicker">Campaign Audit</span>
          <div class="plan__price">₹15,000–₹25,000</div>
          <p class="plan__per">per campaign, quoted in advance</p>
          <ul class="plan__list">
            <li>Up to 5 creatives</li>
            <li>Up to 20 publishers</li>
            <li>Up to 40 episodes</li>
            <li>Historical lookback</li>
            <li>Interactive report viewer</li>
            <li>CSV/JSON export</li>
            <li>PDF audit report</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="plan__note">
            Price scales with number of creatives, publishers, episodes, and
            lookback period. Not included: dynamic ad insertion,
            host-read spots, video sources, legal testimony.
          </p>
          <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">
            Request a Campaign Audit
          </Button>
        </div>

        <div class="card plan plan--muted reveal">
          <span class="kicker">Continuous Monitoring · in development</span>
          <div class="plan__price">Contact us</div>
          <p class="plan__per">waitlist, per-organization</p>
          <ul class="plan__list">
            <li>Continuous campaign monitoring</li>
            <li>Automated discrepancy alerts</li>
            <li>Reconciliation dashboard</li>
            <li>API access</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="plan__note">
            V2 is in development. Join the waitlist and we will contact you
            when it is available.
          </p>
          <Button variant="secondary" href="/contact">
            Join the Waitlist
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="faq">
          <summary>{faq.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq__body">{faq.a}</div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .pricing-grid {
    margin-top: 40px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .plan {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .plan__price {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--indigo);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .plan__per {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .plan .btn {
    width: 100%;
  }
  .plan__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding: 0;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .plan__list li {
    padding: 8px 0 8px 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grey);
    position: relative;
  }
  .plan__list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 16px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--teal);
  }
  .plan__note {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .plan--muted {
    background: var(--off-white);
  }
</style>
